= Cardiac output — Simple =

'''Cardiac output''' is how much blood the heart pumps in one minute.

It depends on two things: how often the heart beats and how much blood the heart pushes out with each beat. Multiplying those numbers gives cardiac output.

A [[Pulse|pulse]] count tells you about the heartbeat rate, but it cannot tell you how much blood moves on every beat. [[Blood pressure]] is also different: it measures pressure, not the volume pumped each minute.

Doctors estimate cardiac output using special measurements when it helps assess circulation.

